WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.252
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
8: Media, Technology, and News.

2
00:00:04.332 --> 00:00:06.892
This unit is called "Media, Technology,

3
00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:14.812
and News" because you will explore how information travels
in the modern world and why it matters to think critically

4
00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:16.572
about everything you read,

5
00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:17.723
watch, and share.

6
00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:25.507
Every day, millions of messages flow through newspapers,
television channels, websites, and social media platforms.

7
00:00:25.587 --> 00:00:29.636
Some of these messages are carefully researched and truthful.

8
00:00:29.716 --> 00:00:33.427
Others are misleading, exaggerated, or completely false.

9
00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:36.676
As a young person growing up in the digital age,

10
00:00:36.756 --> 00:00:44.731
one of the most important skills you can develop is the
ability to tell the difference between reliable information and

11
00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:45.746
misinformation.

12
00:00:45.826 --> 00:00:51.432
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:00:51.512 --> 00:00:53.353
By the end of this unit,

14
00:00:53.433 --> 00:01:01.437
you will be able to explain what media literacy
means and why it is important for young people today.

15
00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:08.480
You will also identify the key features of
a reliable news source and an unreliable one.

16
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:16.803
You will also read a text about media and answer
comprehension and analysis questions in full sentences.

17
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.764
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

18
00:01:19.844 --> 00:01:26.462
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: express,
claim, allege, correspond, explanation, influence.

19
00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:31.629
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

20
00:01:31.709 --> 00:01:35.647
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

21
00:01:35.727 --> 00:01:42.566
The reading sequence includes Media Literacy: Reading
the News with Care and Breaking News at Kilima Academy.

22
00:01:42.646 --> 00:01:43.454
Read actively.

23
00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:47.834
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:47.914 --> 00:01:51.959
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:56.902
The first language focus is Present
Perfect + Just, and Reported Speech.

26
00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:04.248
The present perfect with just announces that something
happened moments ago, which is why news reports say,

27
00:02:04.328 --> 00:02:07.611
"The government has just announced a new policy."

28
00:02:07.691 --> 00:02:13.927
Reported speech then lets a journalist pass on
what someone said without quoting every word.

29
00:02:14.007 --> 00:02:18.389
Together, these two patterns are
the engine room of news English.

30
00:02:18.469 --> 00:02:25.872
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

31
00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:30.705
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Debate: Digital Media Ethics.

32
00:02:30.785 --> 00:02:35.203
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

33
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:38.626
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

34
00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:42.184
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

35
00:02:42.264 --> 00:02:43.894
You are ready to begin.

36
00:02:43.974 --> 00:02:51.252
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

37
00:02:51.332 --> 00:02:54.819
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

38
00:02:54.899 --> 00:03:03.218
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
